SUMMARY:Betty Oliphant Theatre: ProArteDanza (contemporary ballet/dance)  
 $40 promo
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nCertainly one of Toronto's most import
 ant dance groups!!!\n\nWe will join them again (3rd time) for a Sunday aft
 ernoon performance. November 1\n\nhttps://www.proartedanza.com/\n\n*Ticket
  link below*. **OUR** price $40 per ticket.\n\n(Regular price is $55 per t
 icket).\n\n\\*\\*\\*ProArteDanza continues to deliver some of the most vit
 al and rigorously crafted contemporary dance in the country.\n\n*Paula Cit
 ron\, Dance Critic*\n\n**ProArteDanza is a repertory contemporary dance co
 mpany** which challenges and inspires its artists and our audience through
  **bold new work** and invests in the future of the art form through educa
 tional programs.\n​\nCommitted to *“passion in performance”*\, ProAr
 teDanza strives to reach the widest possible audience through an open\, eq
 uitable and inclusive culture which fosters artistic risk-taking\, innovat
 ion and collaboration.\n\nhttps://www.proartedanza.com/copy-of-fall-season
 -2026\n\n**Ticket link here**:\nhttps://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/ticketing/fall
 -2026-season-2\n\nUSE promo code: **MEETUP** for the $40 tickets.\n\n**ONL
 Y** available on the ADULT tickets.\n\n**ALL** tickets purchased will need
  to be ADULT--not the Seniors.\n\n(you can also adjust the 'added donation
 ' tab as needed\n\n**General admission seating**. Venue holds about 250 pe
 ople.\n\nArrive on time/in advance--*WE can all sit together.*\n\nThe Dora
  Award-winning company performs contemporary ballet. By that\, I mean that
  the dancers need ballet training to execute the movement. Technique is im
 portant\, especially when they have to negotiate the intricate and often a
 rduous movement constructed by co-choreographers **Roberto Campanella** an
 d **Robert Glumbek**.
