SUMMARY:The Theatre Centre:  Far-Flung Peoples  ($20-$30)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nThe phone is ringing.\n\nThe roof is b
 anging.\n\nFrench downstairs.\n\nEnglish upstairs.\n\nCaught in the middle
 : five people\, one couch\, and a landlord calling it an open-concept bedr
 oom.\n\n**Welcome to Far-Flung Peoples**\, an award-winning\, fast-paced\,
  multilingual dark comedy set inside a crooked house in downtown Toronto\,
  where its residents are squeezed into a living arrangement that would rai
 se questions at City Hall\, if City Hall were paying attention.\n\n*Ticket
  link is below ($20-$30)*\n\nThe winner of the Norma Epstein Foundation Aw
 ard and the Hamilton Fringe Best New Canadian Play Contest\, *Far-Flung Pe
 oples*\, is funny until it is not.\n\nWe'll join our friends at ***Minor P
 unctuations Theatre*** for this!\n\nhttps://minorpunctuationstheatre.com/o
 ur-team/\n\n**TICKET link is here: (you're purchasing for Sunday November 
 8th @ 2pm)**\n\nhttps://theatrecentre.org/event/far-flung-peoples/\n\nSmal
 l venue space--just 50 seats!! General admission\,\n\nWe'll meet in the CA
 FE before the performance.
